\ Explicit ownership cleanup for all linked lists in this branch.
\ The CAL system library has REMOVE and DEALLOCATE primitives but no
\ catch-all DESTROY routine for an arbitrary "some things" list.
\ A list's nodes must be detached before their memory is deallocated.
\ Clearing dynamically allocated strings prevents stale owned buffers.
\ Never clear a list by merely voiding its first and last pointers.
\ All of these routines have exactly one loop each.

To destroy some gate marks:
  Loop.
    If the gate marks are empty, break.
    Put the gate marks' first into a gate mark.
    Remove the gate mark from the gate marks.
    Deallocate the gate mark.
  Repeat.

